.SH NAME
.PP
getChangeStreamToken \- Get a token for the latest position information of the
change stream for the current node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]Sdb.getChangeStreamToken()\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to get a token for the latest position information of the
change stream for the current node.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
None
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
If the function executes successfully, it will return a StreamToken type object.
.PP
If the function execution fails, it will throw an exception and output error
information.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
When the exception happens, use getLastErrMsg() to get the error message or use
getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v7.2.2 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
// Get the latest position information of the change stream for the current node
var token = db.getChangeStreamToken();
\f[]
.fi
